<h1><img hspace="0" height="32" width="32"
	src="../images/carmenHelpIcons/c3_32.gif" border="0">&nbsp;What
you must keep in mind</h1>
<hr size="2" align="left" width="100%" color="blue">
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h3>Help Files</h3>
<ul>
	<li>You can not use XML&nbsp;files for the Java Help System (not
	supported yet at 2009).</li>
	<li>You must publish the project to generate the Java Help System
	from within Helen.</li>
	<li>You must create one Helen Project for each language you want
	to add with the same structure that the english one and translate it.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Swing Designer and Windows Builder</h3>
<ul>
	<li><b>Bug</b>: Any panel/window/dialog that has a generic type
	element (like type&lt;?&gt;) will fail.
	<ul>
		<li>To solve this, you must comment all the methods that contains
		in the declaration or in the parameters or in the body of the method,
		these types of generic types</li>
		<li>This is because the Swing&nbsp;Designer have been designed
		prior to Java 6 and therefore, it is reading the "&lt;" and "&gt;"
		like its own internal XML&nbsp;attributes and misunderstand them.</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
</body>
